{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuaQtviEFKTiRYRxZTcU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I recorded TC-055 as a **pass** and committed it as `f635727b2`, ending with the `WI: WI-831` trailer. The verdict file's machine line is `OUTCOME: RECORDED result=pass`.\n\nI didn't judge the dashboard myself. The Method needs a critic from a different model family than the dashboard's Claude-written code, and I'm Claude. Instead I checked the six-judge sitting against the Method using its raw files in `review-tmp/2026-10-10-leg01/wi831/`, not the compiled summary:\n\n- **Different family, fresh sessions:** each judge was a separate read-only `gpt-6-luna` session (the logs confirm the model). None opened earlier reviews, logs, work items, observations or `status.md`.\n- **Correct inputs:** each brief had the rubric word for word, the intent rows (SR-054, SN-023/024, LLR-055, TC-055) and the scope lines of every test-bound row with its TC id. No brief had the implementer's self-assessment.\n- **Complete matrix:** the screenshot run exited cleanly with 36 shots and nothing left unshot. The Knowledge tab is missing only because its setting is off in `docs/process.toml`. Each judge's tile list covers the landing view plus the What, When, How, Process and Retired tabs at its width and theme.\n- **Only live anchors cited:** all six verdicts read `APPROVE findings=0 T2=pass T4=pass T5=pass T8=pass`. The rubric's header names T2, T4, T5 and T8 as the live set, and each retired anchor (T1, T3, T6, T7) states in place which test row holds it.\n- **Nothing changed since the render:** the only commit after the judges' render base `c5da1c9` adds their record, so no declared input changed before HEAD.\n- **Spot check:** I looked at four tiles and saw nothing that contradicts the APPROVE. The roadmap wires are faint, which one judge also noted.\n\nThe record is `docs/test/observations/TC-055.2026-10-11T012305Z.toml` and expires 2027-01-09.\n\nI left the coordinator's `002-ADJUDICATE-c145ac6.md.requested` file untracked and untouched.\n\nMy first commit put a blank line between `WI: WI-831` and `Co-Authored-By`, so git's trailer parser (`agent_common.py:738`) couldn't see it. I amended that unpushed commit to put the trailer in the final block, and git now finds it. The judges' own commit `c145ac6` doesn't carry the trailer either, which is expected because it isn't a recorded judgement."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":679,"cache_read_input_tokens":84559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":679},"output_tokens":772,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd9b4695-02c1-4b3f-9b22-de5853423d28","uuid":"a4110bf5-b717-44f7-b172-7678447cdb12","timestamp":"2026-10-11T01:24:37.743Z","request_id":"req_011CfuaQt1PgMsYHwPvEfsuU"}
